This assertion checks that the value of `New_Ret` is greater than or equal to zero. If `New_Ret` is not a non-negative integer, the assertion will fail, potentially helping to catch potential issues in the code. But note that Debug.Assert does not work in Release configuration hence we would need to guard it with #if DEBUG.

```cs
#if DEBUG
    Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0, "Count value of array is either 0 or greater than or equal to one.");
#endif
```

The additional string argument provides a message that will be displayed if the assertion fails which clarifies the failure point, making debugging easier. Please ensure that you are running this code in the debug mode and have enabled the "Just My Code" feature in your Visual Studio for this to work correctly.--------------------```cs
